/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - Use a plane truss.
   - m members; r reactions; j joints; D degree.
   - D = 0 means determinate: equilibrium gives every force.
   - The method rests on the ideal truss: straight members joined by frictionless pins, loads applied only at the joints, and self-weight neglected or lumped at the joints.
   - Assume tension positive: member force pulls its joint away.
   - At an unloaded joint, two non-collinear members carry zero force.
   - If D > 0, one compatibility condition per redundant is needed.
   - Call the force in the redundant member X.
   - U is the strain energy of all members including the redundant one; X is the redundant force; n is ∂N/∂X.
   - A matrix program gives every force and deflection at once.
*/
